{
  "_": [
    "deadpool_pro on jpsalas's 'JP's Deadpool' 6.10 (VPForums): a Pro's playfield.",
    "Its DEAD and POOL targets are standups (the LE's are two 4-bank drops) and it has",
    "no up/down ramp, so the Pro is the card it fits (`preferred`; the two cards number",
    "every switch the same, the LE adds the drop banks' and ramp's coils). Switches",
    "matched by PLACE: the table's objects fitted to the Pro's switch_xy drawing",
    "(drawing x = (table x + 66) / 3.3, y = (table y + 133) / 3.33; every rollover,",
    "target, spinner, pop and saucer lands within ~12 drawing units of its switch), then",
    "checked against what each hit sub does. Lights matched the same way to led_io.txt",
    "(most within 4 units); the GI LEDs are the LE's names (BOTTOM / MID LEFT / MID",
    "RIGHT / UPPER LEFT / UPPER RIGHT GI), which the Pro's device table leaves out, so",
    "every gi light is a GUESS by region. The Katana Handle lock lane is one kicker in",
    "the table and LOCK 1-4 on the machine: the kicker feeds a four-ball stack on them,",
    "and the LOCK POST, which the game holds down for as long as it wants balls out (12 s",
    "at a multiball), lets one out every 600 ms while it is down (PAD-901)."
  ],
  "title": "deadpool_pro",
  "model": "Pro",
  "preferred": true,
  "detect": [
    "JP's Deadpool",
    "jpsdeadpool"
  ],
  "output": "JP's Deadpool v610 (PAD).vpx",
  "table": {"name": "JP's Deadpool 6.10", "by": "jpsalas", "where": "VPForums"},
  "solenoid_max": 68,
